":"Other study-specific measure","Compared with":"Parent vs child report","Statistic type":"Correlation","Result":"Time since first account: parent vs adolescent r = .74, p < .001","Direction":"Not reported"},{"Study_ID":"FT0156","Source":"Barry 2017","Measure":"Other study-specific measure","Compared with":"Parent vs child report","Statistic type":"Both","Result":"Parental monitoring: r = .69; parents reported more monitoring than adolescents (M 1.71 vs 1.64, p = .045)","Direction":"Not reported"},{"Study_ID":"FT0221","Source":"Orben 2019","Measure":"Activity checklist · social media activities","Compared with":"Diary","Statistic type":"Correlation","Result":"Irish: r = .18; US: r = .08 (weekday), .05 (weekend); UK: r = .18","Direction":"Not reported"},{"Study_ID":"FT0243","Source":"Fors 2019","Measure":"ABCD Youth Screen Time Survey (STQ)","Compared with":"Parent vs child report","Statistic type":"Both","Result":"Child-parent agreement beta = .18 weekday, .16 weekend; children reported more EMU than parents","Direction":"Over-report"},{"Study_ID":"FT0348","Source":"Wade 2021","Measure":"Single item · social media duration · weekday/weekend","Compared with":"Device logs","Statistic type":"Both","Result":"child r=0.49 (95% CI 0.28-0.66); 79% (53/66) reported less than sensed","Direction":"Under-report"},{"Study_ID":"FT0348","Source":"Wade 2021","Measure":"Single item · social media duration · weekday/weekend","Compared with":"Device logs","Statistic type":"Both","Result":"parent r=-0.06 post-sensing; 58% (39/67) reported less, 42% more","Direction":"No consistent direction"},{"Study_ID":"FT0352","Source":"Verbeij 2021","Measure":"Platform checklist · frequency or time per platform","Compared with":"Device logs","Statistic type":"Both","Result":"mean overestimate 6 h 37 min/week (d=.60); between-person r=.59","Direction":"Over-report"},{"Study_ID":"FT0352","Source":"Verbeij 2021","Measure":"Platform checklist · frequency or time per platform","Compared with":"Device logs","Statistic type":"Both","Result":"mean overestimate 6 h 59 min/week (d=.39); between-person r=.65","Direction":"Over-report"},{"Study_ID":"FT0352","Source":"Verbeij 2021","Measure":"EMA prompts · study-specific social media items","Compared with":"Device logs","Statistic type":"Both","Result":"mean overestimate 7 min 37 s/hour (d=.91); between-person r=.55; within-person r=.32","Direction":"Over-report"},{"Study_ID":"FT0372","Source":"Paschke 2021","Measure":"Social Media Use Disorder Scale for Adolescents","Compared with":"Parent vs child report","Statistic type":"Correlation","Result":"r = 0.54 (SOMEDIS-A self-report vs SMDS-P parent report)","Direction":"Not reported"},{"Study_ID":"FT0426","Source":"Austermann 2021","Measure":"Social Media Disorder Scale – Parent version (SMDS-P)","Compared with":"Parent vs child report","Statistic type":"Both","Result":"SMDS-P vs adolescent SMDS: r = 0.68; kappa = 0.51","Direction":"Not reported"},{"Study_ID":"FT0446","Source":"Verbeij 2022","Measure":"EMA prompts · study-specific social media items","Compared with":"Device logs","Statistic type":"Both","Result":"r = 0.44 (between), r = 0.30 (within); mean 13.77 vs 5.87 min/h, d = 0.74","Direction":"Over-report"},{"Study_ID":"FT0470","Source":"Paschke 2022","Measure":"Social Media Use Disorder Scale for Parents (SOMEDIS-P)","Compared with":"Parent vs child report","Statistic type":"Both","Result":"r = 0.66 (total score); κ = 0.44 (SMUD classification), 95.02% concordance","Direction":"Not reported"},{"Study_ID":"FT0480","Source":"Nagata 2022","Measure":"Single item · daily social media duration · typical day","Compared with":"Parent vs child report","Statistic type":"Both","Result":"Social media: parent 0.89 h vs adolescent 0.98 h, difference -0.09 h (95% CI -0.14, -0.03); ICC = 0.34 (0.30, 0.38)","Direction":"Under-report"},{"Study_ID":"FT0480","Source":"Nagata 2022","Measure":"Single item · daily social media duration · typical day","Compared with":"Parent vs child report","Statistic type":"Both","Result":"Texting: parent 1.16 h vs adolescent 0.84 h, difference 0.32 h (0.26, 0.37); ICC = 0.29 (0.25, 0.34)","Direction":"Over-report"},{"Study_ID":"FT0480","Source":"Nagata 2022","Measure":"Single item · daily social media duration · typical day","Compared with":"Parent vs child report","Statistic type":"Both","Result":"Video chatting: parent 0.95 h vs adolescent 0.65 h, difference 0.31 h (0.26, 0.35); ICC = 0.32 (0.29, 0.36)","Direction":"Over-report"},{"Study_ID":"FT0480","Source":"Nagata 2022","Measure":"Single item · daily social media duration · typical day","Compared with":"Parent vs child report","Statistic type":"Both","Result":"Total recreational screen time: parent 4.46 h vs adolescent 3.87 h, difference 0.58 h (0.47, 0.69); ICC = 0.43 (0.39, 0.46)","Direction":"Over-report"},{"Study_ID":"FT0487","Source":"Marsh 2022","Measure":"Social Integration and Emotional Connection to social media (SMUIS-SIEC subscale)","Compared with":"Parent vs child report","Statistic type":"Correlation","Result":"r = 0.45, p < 0.001","Direction":"Not reported"},{"Study_ID":"FT0538","Source":"Bagot 2022","Measure":"ABCD Youth Screen Time Survey (STQ)","Compared with":"Parent vs child report","Statistic type":"Agreement","Result":"Year 2 total screen time, weekday: child 196.97 vs parent 182.57 min (t = 4.58, p<.001); weekend: child 310.43 vs parent 274.26 min (t = 9.30, p<.001); parents report less than children","Direction":"Under-report"},{"Study_ID":"FT0538","Source":"Bagot 2022","Measure":"Single item · social media duration · weekday/weekend","Compared with":"Parent vs child report","Statistic type":"Agreement","Result":"Year 2 total screen time, weekday: child 196.97 vs parent 182.57 min (t = 4.58, p<.001); weekend: child 310.43 vs parent 274.26 min (t = 9.30, p<.001); parents report less than children","Direction":"Under-report"},{"Study_ID":"FT0549","Source":"Ye 2023","Measure":"Other study-specific measure","Compared with":"Parent vs child 